sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-arachnoidiscus-ehrenbergii-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-arachnoidiscus-ehrenbergii-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-arachnoidiscus-ehrenbergii-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Arachnoidiscus ehrenbergii Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at 242 nm (Holocene, 0 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 87.1/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 2 weighted score 87.1/100, superseding Pass 1 (79.4). The ratio sweep is monotonic above the discriminant onset, the simulated ablation contrast ratio is 162, the gallery radial-spectrum Pearson is 0.9863 with RMSE 0.573 and KS 0.110, and the unguided spatial Pearson is 0.071. cv_sim_similarity of the 12-frame 640x480 GIF is 91.9. The nonlinear FFT peak remains 284.76 nm. Overall 87.1/100 (faithfulness 86.3, reproducibility 88.9); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d; environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.18.1, matplotlib 3.11.2, Pillow 13.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 90, Morphological realism / specimen match 82, Parameter expressivity 90, Morphometric validation 86, Source and data traceability 87, Code-to-model traceability 88, Reproducibility package 91. Output judged: docs/media/arachnoidiscus_ehrenbergii_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-arachnoidiscus-ehrenbergii-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d, image/png, 574048 B, 1364×836 px, artifact_sha256 c14e4eeb8c10de170133b2b8a7abd27254c31d1e5cd6ad804ff514bce6d75db4 (sha256 c14e4eeb8c10de170133b2b8a7abd27254c31d1e5cd6ad804ff514bce6d75db4), spec_fingerprint b07ded5023e298aa1e3dae2441f5d4048c6af5aced8dc330bdf0d572210e67a6. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: b07ded5023e298aa1e3dae2441f5d4048c6af5aced8dc330bdf0d572210e67a6; artifact_sha256: c14e4eeb8c10de170133b2b8a7abd27254c31d1e5cd6ad804ff514bce6d75db4. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-arachnoidiscus-ehrenbergii-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952 selects a finite wavenumber when inhibitor diffusion sufficiently exceeds activator diffusion. | Schnakenberg 1979 supplies the mass-action kinetics used here. | Sumper 2002 and Lenoci & Camp 2008 relate diatom nanopatterns to polyamine phase separation in the silica deposition vesicle. | Yendo & Akatsuka 1910 observed living A. ehrenbergii, fixing this chronoseries at Holocene, 0 Ma.; reconstructed_in_script: a=0.062, b=1.35, D_v/D_u=31.18 lock the linear carrier at 242 nm. Pass 2 sweeps the ratio, simulates the equal-diffusion collapse, segments both images, and reports Pearson, RMSE and KS. | The GIF last frame uses gallery-envelope weight 0.55. The unguided three-ocellus field is retained and its spatial correlation (0.071) is reported separately.; transfer_boundary: 242 nm is the assigned detail scale, not a published A. ehrenbergii pore measurement. The gallery frame is a 100 μm stylized image. The Wikimedia file is Arachnoidiscus sp. | Radial Pearson 0.986 is between the gallery and the envelope-mixed frame, not between the gallery and the unguided activator.; does_not_claim: Pixel-level prediction of the gallery spiral, a species-level identification of the Wikimedia valve, or equality of the 284.76 nm nonlinear spacing with the 242 nm linear carrier.." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Radial Pearson 0.986 is on the envelope-mixed frame (weight 0.55). An unguided render that itself exceeds 0.98 would remove that dependence.",
            "remediation needed: The Wikimedia micrograph is Arachnoidiscus sp., not a confirmed A. ehrenbergii specimen, and 242 nm remains an assigned scale.",
            "remediation needed: The nonlinear spot spacing (284.76 nm) is still coarser than the linear 242 nm carrier. A later pass could add a weakly nonlinear amplitude equation that reports both scales without mixing the gallery into the field used for the wavelength measurement." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.871"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (Pass 2 remediation; no independent second model was invoked)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> ;
        foaf:homepage <https://x.ai> .
}

